Article 5 (Decision on Selection)
(1) The Minister of National Defense shall select as legal officers persons who meet all of the following requirements, ascertaining whether they meet each requirement in the order listed. In such cases, the Minister of National Defense shall determine matters necessary for the application methods, application period, etc. for legal officers. [Amended on November 29, 2016, and October 1, 2025.]
1. A person whose information was notified under Article 2 and whose physical grade is Grade I, II, or III;
2. A person who has passed document screening under Article 4 (3);
3. A person who has applied to the Minister of National Defense to become a legal officer;
4. A person who meets the following respective academic-performance criteria:
(a) For a person scheduled to complete the Judicial Research and Training Institute program: Selection in descending order of average grades at the Judicial Research and Training Institute;
(b) For a person who has graduated from a law school: Selection in descending order of average grades at the law school.
(2) Where the number of persons who have applied to become legal officers under paragraph (1) 3 falls short of the number of legal officers to be selected under Article 3, the Minister of National Defense shall select the shortfall from among persons who have not applied to become legal officers (limited to persons who meet the requirements in paragraph (1) 1 and 2), by means of a public computerized drawing of lots. In such cases, the shortfall shall be selected separately for each selection category under the latter sentence of Article 3 (1). [Amended on October 1, 2025.]
(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), where the number of persons whose physical grades are Grades I through III falls short of the number of legal officers to be selected under Article 3, the Minister of National Defense shall select the shortfall from among persons with physical Grade IV, by means of a public computerized drawing of lots. In such cases, the shortfall shall be selected separately for each selection category under the latter sentence of Article 3 (1). [Amended on November 29, 2016, and October 1, 2025.]
